-- title:
--   Generic flatness over a Noetherian domain
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian integral domain, let $B$ be a commutative $A$-algebra of finite type, and let $M$ be an additive abelian group carrying compatible $A$- and $B$-module structures (the $A$-action being the restriction of the $B$-action along $A \to B$, as a scalar tower) such that $M$ is finitely generated as a $B$-module. The assertion is that there exists $a \in A$ with $a \neq 0$ such that the $A$-module $$\mathrm{Localization}\big(\text{powers of } \mathrm{algebraMap}_{A,B}(a)\big) \otimes_B M,$$ that is, the base change of $M$ along the localisation of $B$ at the multiplicative submonoid generated by the image of $a$ in $B$, is flat over $A$. Note that flatness is asserted over $A$ itself, not over the localisation $A[1/a]$ (the two are equivalent here), and that freeness, which the classical statement also provides, is not asserted.
--
--   This is the module form of Grothendieck's generic flatness (generic freeness) lemma. It is used to produce flat loci: it underlies the statement that the set of primes of $A$ at which a localisation of $M$ is flat is open, the existence of a nonempty flat preimage for a locally finite type morphism over a reduced base, and faithful flatness of Hopf algebras over an algebraically closed field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Flat_exists_ne_zero_flat_localization_tensorProduct.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open TensorProduct in

theorem Module.Flat.exists_ne_zero_flat_localization_tensorProduct
    {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M]
    [Module.Finite B M] :
    ∃ a : A, a ≠ 0 ∧
      Module.Flat A (Localization (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap A B a)) ⊗[B] M) := by sorry
